{
  "_comment": [
    "The Tor pins of record (TOR_BUNDLE_DISTRIBUTION.md TB-9). One file, two readers:",
    "rust/shekyl-tor-control-client/build.rs compiles the row for the build target into the",
    "binary, and scripts/release/tor_bundle.py fetches, checks and stages the bundle for",
    "packaging. Nothing reads this file at runtime. Change it only through the",
    "RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md 'Bundled Tor pin current' procedure: a digest recorded here must",
    "come from a tarball whose signature was verified against signing_key_fingerprint.",
    "Every target the release builds has exactly one row, pinned or unavailable",
    "(scripts/ci/check_tor_pin_targets.py). An unavailable row is a ruling unless it",
    "carries \"pending\": the identifier of the work that will pin it. A pending row",
    "compiles as unavailable, which is what the binary does today, and is printed by",
    "the gate on every run: an unavailable target is a gap to close (TB-4), and a node",
    "on one announces that it has no managed Tor; it is never refused (TB-2).",
    "A row may carry \"switched_off\": the record of a ruling that took its target out",
    "of the release matrix (riscv64 Linux: CA-1). No descriptor builds it; the row stays",
    "so a source build of that target still compiles, and the gate prints it every run.",
    "A macOS row carries two digest sets (TB-11): files, the Developer ID-signed bytes",
    "that ship and that the binary checks, and upstream, Tor's own as extracted from",
    "the tarball. tor_bundle.py ties them: every byte outside the code signature is Tor's."
  ],
